---
id: org.dxos.plugin.qa
name: QaPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A store for QA results. A `TestPlan` declares a set of `TestCase`s; each execution of the plan
appends a `TestRun` to the plan's feed, carrying one `TestResult` per case together with the
documents, screenshots and recordings that evidence it. Plans are authored and results are pushed
by an agent over the DXOS MCP surface, so the same plan a human reads in Composer is the one a
`flow QA-n` run reports against.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`   |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`          |
| `skill`     | `org.dxos.mdl.skill@1.0`       |
| `flow`      | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0`        |
| `step`      | `org.dxos.mdl.step@1.0`        |

## Ontology

Three ECHO objects and three inline structs. The split is deliberate:

- **`TestCase` is an object** because a case outlives any one plan revision — results across
  months of runs point at the same case, and coverage questions ("has QA-3 ever passed on main?")
  are queries over that identity.
- **`TestRun` is an object** because it is the feed entry: the plan owns a `Feed<TestRun>`, so a
  run is appended, never mutated in place by a later run.
- **`TestResult` is a struct nested in its run**, not an object. A result has no life outside the
  run that produced it and is never referenced from elsewhere; making it an object would double
  the object count per run for no query anyone asks.
- **There is no artifact type.** An artifact is a `Ref` to whatever the artifact already is — a
  `Document`, a `File`, a recording — plus a caption at the reference site.

```
TestPlan ──cases[]──▶ TestCase
    └── feed ─▶ Feed<TestRun>
                    TestRun ──plan──▶ TestPlan
                        └── results[]  (TestResult)  ──case──▶ TestCase
                                └── steps[] (TestStepResult)
                                └── artifacts[] ──▶ Ref<Document | File | …>
```

## Types

```mdl
type TestResultStatus
  desc: >
    A terminal outcome — the only thing a case or a step can be reported as. `blocked` is distinct
    from `failed`: nothing was tested, so it must not be counted as a defect.
  literals: passed | failed | skipped | blocked
```

```mdl
type TestStatus
  desc: >
    A run's status: any terminal outcome, or `running` while it is open. `running` is deliberately
    absent from TestResultStatus — a case result that could be `running` would be counted as
    non-failing by the rollup, and a run could seal as `passed` with nothing actually finished.
  literals: TestResultStatus | running
```

```mdl
type TestStep
  desc: One move in a case — the authored instruction and its criterion. Mirrors `step` in the QA dialect.
  fields:
    id?: string                # stable handle; steps are otherwise numbered by position from 1
    do: string                 # the human instruction
    expect: string             # the criterion both a human and an agent judge
```

```mdl
type TestCase
  desc: >
    The definition of one test. Stored with typename org.dxos.type.qa.test-case v0.1.0.
    Static — an execution never writes here.
  fields:
    key: string                # stable human id, e.g. "QA-3"; unique within a plan
    title: string
    description?: string
    steps: TestStep[]
    tags?: string[]
    source?: DXN               # the spec this case was authored from (a PLUGIN.mdl document)
```

```mdl
type TestPlan
  desc: >
    Root ECHO object and the container the UI opens. Stored with typename
    org.dxos.type.qa.test-plan v0.1.0.
  fields:
    name: string
    description?: string
    cases: Ref<TestCase>[]     # ordered; the plan owns the ordering, the case does not
    feed: Ref<Feed<TestRun>>   # durable append-only log of executions (SetParent)
    source?: DXN               # the `## QA` section this plan tracks, when generated from a spec
```

```mdl
type Actor
  desc: >
    Not defined here — `Actor` from @dxos/types (name / email / identityDid / contact / role),
    the same type a Message sender uses. A run's runner is a person or an agent like any other
    actor in the system, so it takes that type rather than a QA-local convention string.
  extends: [org.dxos.types.Actor]
```

```mdl
type TestTarget
  desc: >
    What a run was executed against. The field people filter on six months later, so it is
    structured rather than prose.
  fields:
    ref?: string               # git sha, tag, or PR number
    branch?: string
    url?: string               # deployed app under test
    env?: string               # "local" | "preview" | "prod" | free-form
```

```mdl
type TestArtifactRef
  desc: >
    A reference to evidence. Not a type of its own — the target is whatever the artifact already
    is (Document, File, recording), and only the caption and kind live here.
  fields:
    kind: screenshot | video | log | document | other
    caption?: string
    target: Ref<any>           # Document, File, …
```

```mdl
type TestStepResult
  desc: Per-step outcome within a TestResult. Positional — index n corresponds to TestCase.steps[n].
  fields:
    status: TestResultStatus
    note?: string              # why it failed, or the constraint that blocked it
    artifacts?: TestArtifactRef[]
```

```mdl
type TestResult
  desc: >
    The outcome of one TestCase within one TestRun. An inline struct of TestRun.results — never
    an object of its own.
  fields:
    case: Ref<TestCase>
    status: TestResultStatus
    steps?: TestStepResult[]
    note?: string              # failure summary, or `blocked` reason (QA dialect Rule 9)
    durationMs?: number
    artifacts?: TestArtifactRef[]   # evidence for the case as a whole
```

```mdl
type TestRun
  desc: >
    One execution of a plan, appended to TestPlan.feed. Stored with typename
    org.dxos.type.qa.test-run v0.1.0. Results accumulate as the run proceeds; `status` is a
    rollup, written when the run is finished.
  fields:
    plan: Ref<TestPlan>
    status: TestStatus         # `running` until finished; then the rollup below
    cases: string[]            # case keys the run set out to cover, captured at startRun
    target?: TestTarget
    runner?: Actor             # who ran it — `Actor` from @dxos/types, not a QA-local string
    stages?: string[]          # which of before/test/after actually ran (QA dialect Rule 8)
    startedAt: string          # ISO-8601
    finishedAt?: string
    results: TestResult[]
    summary?: string           # one-paragraph verdict, for the feed row
  note: >
    The rollup runs over `cases`, not over `results`: a key in `cases` with no result counts as
    `skipped`. Rolling up over `results` alone would seal a run that reported nothing as `passed`.
    Precedence is failed > blocked > skipped > passed, and an empty `cases` is `skipped` before
    that precedence is consulted — otherwise a run covering nothing would fall through to
    `passed`. So `passed` requires a non-empty capture in which every case reported `passed`.
    `cases` is also the authority for `pushResult`: what the run may report on is what it
    captured, not what the plan currently holds.
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Author and maintain plans

  req F-1.1: A TestPlan can be created empty, or generated from the `## QA` section of a
    PLUGIN.mdl — each `flow QA-n` becoming a TestCase whose `key` is the flow id and whose steps
    are the flow's `test` stage.
  req F-1.2: Cases are added, updated, reordered and removed through operations, so an agent over
    MCP edits a plan without touching ECHO directly.
  req F-1.3: Re-generating a plan from an updated spec matches existing cases by `key` and updates
    them in place, so historical results keep pointing at the same TestCase.

feat F-2: Record runs

  req F-2.1: Starting a run appends a TestRun with status `running` to the plan's feed and returns
    its id; every later push names that id.
  req F-2.2: A result is pushed per case, incrementally, so a long run is observable while it is
    still going.
  req F-2.3: Finishing a run computes `status` as a rollup over the case keys captured at
    `startRun` — `skipped` if the capture is empty, else `failed` if any failed, else `blocked` if
    any is blocked, else `skipped` if any case went unreported, else `passed` — and stamps
    `finishedAt`. A run that covered nothing, or reported nothing, therefore seals as `skipped`;
    `passed` is reachable only from a non-empty capture in which every case reported `passed`.
  req F-2.4: A run is immutable once finished; a correction is a new run, not an edit.

feat F-3: Evidence

  req F-3.1: An artifact is attached by reference to an existing object; the plugin never copies
    or stores bytes of its own.
  req F-3.2: Artifacts attach at step granularity as well as case granularity.

feat F-4: Read the history

  req F-4.1: The plan surface shows the feed newest-first, one row per run, with its target and
    pass/fail counts.
  req F-4.2: A case surface shows that case's outcome across every run, so a flaky or long-broken
    case is visible without opening runs one by one.

feat F-5: Agent access over MCP

  req F-5.1: A `QaSkill` names the plan-editing and result-pushing operations in its `tools`, which
    is what makes them reachable from `queryOperations` / `invokeOperation`.
  req F-5.2: Every operation takes ids and plain values only — no live ECHO objects cross the MCP
    boundary.
  req F-5.3: Mutation hints are declared per operation so a host can distinguish reading history
    from writing it.
```

## Operations

```mdl
op createPlan
  key: org.dxos.operation.qa.createPlan
  desc: Creates a TestPlan with its feed. A factory — the caller places the object.
  input:
    name: string
    description?: string
    source?: string            # DXN of the spec document this plan tracks
  output: { plan: TestPlan }
  effects: [echo:write]
  requires: [Database.Service]
```

```mdl
op upsertCase
  key: org.dxos.operation.qa.upsertCase
  desc: >
    Creates or updates a case by `key` within a plan, appending it to `cases` when new. Matching
    on `key` rather than id is what makes re-generation from a spec non-destructive (F-1.3).
  input:
    planId: string
    key: string
    title: string
    description?: string
    steps: TestStep[]
    tags?: string[]
  output: { case: TestCase, created: boolean }
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op removeCase
  key: org.dxos.operation.qa.removeCase
  desc: Removes a case from the plan's `cases`. Past results still reference the TestCase object.
  input:
    planId: string
    key: string
  output: { removed: boolean }
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op reorderCases
  key: org.dxos.operation.qa.reorderCases
  desc: Sets the plan's case ordering.
  input:
    planId: string
    keys: string[]             # the full ordering; unknown or missing keys are an error
  output: { plan: TestPlan }
  errors:
    UnknownCaseError: a key in the ordering is not in the plan
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op startRun
  key: org.dxos.operation.qa.startRun
  desc: >
    Appends a `running` TestRun to the plan's feed and returns its id. Captures the plan's case
    keys onto the run, so a later edit to the plan cannot change what this run was measured
    against. `cases` narrows that capture for a partial run; its keys are validated against the
    plan here, which is the only point at which the plan has a say in a run's coverage.
  input:
    planId: string
    cases?: string[]           # case keys to cover; defaults to the plan's full case list
    target?: TestTarget
    runner?: Actor
    stages?: string[]
  output: { runId: string, cases: string[] }
  errors:
    UnknownCaseError: a requested key is not in the plan
    DuplicateCaseError: a key appears twice in `cases`, which would double-count it in the rollup
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op pushResult
  key: org.dxos.operation.qa.pushResult
  desc: >
    Appends (or replaces, by case key) one TestResult on a running run. Artifacts are given as
    DXNs of objects that already exist.
  input:
    runId: string
    caseKey: string
    status: TestResultStatus
    steps?: TestStepResult[]
    note?: string
    durationMs?: number
    artifacts?: { kind: string, caption?: string, target: string }[]   # target is a DXN
  output: { result: TestResult }
  errors:
    RunFinishedError: the run is already finished and is immutable
    UnknownCaseError: >
      caseKey is not in the run's captured `cases`. Validated against the capture, not against
      the plan's current membership: a `removeCase` mid-run must not reject a result for a case
      the run is still counting as unreported.
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op finishRun
  key: org.dxos.operation.qa.finishRun
  desc: >
    Rolls up `status` over the run's captured `cases`, stamps `finishedAt`, and seals the run.
    A captured case with no result counts as `skipped`, so an empty or partial run cannot seal as
    `passed`.
  input:
    runId: string
    summary?: string
  output: { run: TestRun, unreported: string[] }   # case keys that never received a result
  errors:
    RunFinishedError: the run is already sealed
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op queryRuns
  key: org.dxos.operation.qa.queryRuns
  desc: Reads the plan's feed, newest-first, with optional filters. Results are summarised unless `full`.
  input:
    planId: string
    limit?: number
    status?: TestStatus
    caseKey?: string           # runs containing a result for this case
    full?: boolean             # include per-step detail and artifact refs
  output: { runs: TestRun[] }
  effects: []
```

```mdl
op caseHistory
  key: org.dxos.operation.qa.caseHistory
  desc: One case's status across runs, newest-first — the query behind F-4.2.
  input:
    planId: string
    caseKey: string
    limit?: number
  output: { entries: { runId: string, status: TestStatus, target?: TestTarget, at: string }[] }
  effects: []
```

## Skill

```mdl
skill QaSkill
  key: org.dxos.skill.qa
  desc: >
    Makes the QA store reachable over the DXOS MCP surface: an agent generates a plan from a
    spec's `## QA` section, runs the flows, and pushes a run back as it goes.
  depends_on:
    - org.dxos.skill.database   # query / load, for resolving plans and artifact targets
    - org.dxos.skill.markdown   # authoring the report document an artifact points at
  contributes:
    - plugin-qa/createPlan
    - plugin-qa/upsertCase
    - plugin-qa/removeCase
    - plugin-qa/reorderCases
    - plugin-qa/startRun
    - plugin-qa/pushResult
    - plugin-qa/finishRun
    - plugin-qa/queryRuns
    - plugin-qa/caseHistory
  instructions: >
    Authored in `src/skills/qa/skill.ts`. Covers the run protocol (start once, push per case,
    finish exactly once), the rule that a finished run is never edited, that `blocked` is used
    where a step could not run at all, and that artifacts are attached by DXN to objects the
    agent created first — never inlined.
```

## Components

```mdl
component TestPlanArticle
  desc: Main surface for a plan — the case list above the run feed.
  props:
    subject: TestPlan
    role: "article" | "section"
  state:
    runs: AtomQuery            # the plan's feed, newest-first
  actions:
    openRun(runId: string)
    openCase(caseId: string)
  layout: |
    ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │ Plan name                    [Run] [•••]   │
    ├────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    │ QA-1  Create and open a document      ✓    │
    │ QA-2  Link two documents              ✗    │
    ├────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    │ Runs                                       │
    │ ● 2026-08-31  main@a1b2c3   7/8   qa-flow  │
    │ ● 2026-08-30  main@9f0e1d   8/8   agent    │
    └────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component TestRunArticle
  desc: One run — the per-case result table, each row expanding to steps and artifacts.
  props:
    subject: TestRun
  actions:
    toggleResult(caseKey: string)
    openArtifact(ref: Ref<any>)
```

```mdl
component TestCaseArticle
  desc: One case — its authored steps, and its outcome across every run (F-4.2).
  props:
    subject: TestCase
  state:
    history: { runId: string, status: TestStatus, at: string }[]
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: A run rolls up to the worst outcome
  given: a plan with three cases, and a started run
  when: results are pushed as passed, blocked, passed
  then: finishRun sets the run status to blocked, not passed

test T-2: A failure dominates a block
  given: a started run
  when: results are pushed as failed and blocked
  then: finishRun sets the run status to failed

test T-3: A run covering nothing seals as skipped
  given: a plan with no cases
  when: a run is started and finished without pushing anything
  then: the run status is skipped
  note: the same holds for startRun called with cases: [] on a plan that has cases

test T-4: An unreported case cannot seal as passed
  given: a run started over three cases
  when: one result is pushed as passed and the run is finished
  then: the run status is skipped, and `unreported` names the two cases that never reported

test T-5: A finished run is immutable
  given: a finished run
  when: pushResult is invoked for one of its cases
  then: it fails with RunFinishedError and the run is unchanged

test T-6: Re-generation preserves case identity
  given: a plan whose case QA-1 has results in two past runs
  when: upsertCase is invoked with key QA-1 and a changed title
  then: the same TestCase object is updated, and both past results still resolve to it

test T-7: Artifacts are references, not copies
  given: a Document in the space
  when: a result is pushed with that document as an artifact
  then: the result holds a Ref to the existing object and no new object is created

test T-8: A mid-run plan edit does not reject a captured case
  given: a run started over cases QA-1 and QA-2
  when: QA-2 is removed from the plan, then a result for QA-2 is pushed
  then: the push succeeds — the capture, not the plan, decides what the run may report
```

## QA

```mdl
flow QA-1: Record a run against a plan
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1, F-2.1, F-2.2, F-2.3, F-4.1]
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - collection: a collection in the open space, to create into
    - no TestPlan named "Smoke" exists in the space
  before:
    - name: Create the plan
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose QA Plan. Name it "Smoke".
      invoke: [op:createPlan] { name: "Smoke" }
      capture: plan
      expect: a TestPlan named "Smoke" exists and its feed is empty
      note: Coalesced with the placement below — the created object is live and cannot cross a snippet boundary.
    - name: Place it in the collection
      do: (no separate gesture — the navtree action places it)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: $plan.plan, target: $given.collection }
      expect: "Smoke" appears as a row under the collection
    - name: Add a case
      do: In the plan, click "Add case" and enter key "QA-1", title "It boots".
      invoke: [op:upsertCase] { planId: $plan.plan.id, key: "QA-1", title: "It boots", steps: [{ do: "Open the app", expect: "the app renders" }] }
      expect: the case list shows one row, QA-1
  test:
    - name: Start a run
      do: Click "Run" on the plan.
      invoke: [op:startRun] { planId: $plan.plan.id, runner: { name: "qa-flow", role: "assistant" } }
      capture: run
      expect: a run row appears in the feed with status `running`
      assert: return typeof $run.runId === 'string'
    - name: Push a result
      do: Mark QA-1 as passed in the run view.
      invoke: [op:pushResult] { runId: $run.runId, caseKey: "QA-1", status: "passed" }
      expect: the run row shows 1/1 while still `running`
    - name: Finish the run
      do: Click "Finish" on the run.
      invoke: [op:finishRun] { runId: $run.runId }
      expect: the run status becomes `passed` and `finishedAt` is set
    - name: Reject a late push
      do: Try to mark QA-1 as failed on the finished run.
      invoke: [op:pushResult] { runId: $run.runId, caseKey: "QA-1", status: "failed" }
      expect: the push is rejected with RunFinishedError and the run still reads `passed`
  after:
    - name: Delete the plan
      do: Right-click "Smoke" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$plan.plan], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if open
```

## Open questions

1. **Does a plan pin its cases by revision?** Today `TestCase` is mutable and a past result points
   at its current text, so a re-worded case silently re-writes what an old run appears to have
   tested. The alternative — snapshotting the case's steps into the `TestResult` — costs bytes per
   run but makes history honest. Deferred, not decided.
2. **Where do plans come from in CI?** The MCP path covers an agent at a desk. A CI job pushing
   runs needs either the same operations behind an EDGE-hosted MCP server or a thin ingest
   endpoint; the ontology is the same either way.
3. **Suites.** `TestPlan.cases` is flat. Grouping arrives as either nested plans or a `group` field
   on the case; flat is correct until a real plan is large enough to hurt.

---

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

Extension block types not redefined here (`type`, `feat`, `test`, `component`, `op`, `skill`,
`flow`, `step`) follow the shared DXOS MDL extension library — `op@1.1`, `flow@1.0` and `step@1.0`
are defined in [`packages/reflect/deus/lang/qa.mdl`](../../reflect/deus/lang/qa.mdl); `skill@1.0`
in [`packages/plugins/plugin-crm/PLUGIN.mdl`](../plugin-crm/PLUGIN.mdl); the remainder in
[`packages/reflect/deus/lang/PLUGIN-.template.mdl`](../../reflect/deus/lang/PLUGIN-.template.mdl).
